{"kind":"assert","text":"LL-1 ruling, answer to df7515e2. Hugh, 22 November 20:17 EST: progress LL-1 and PB-3 so that live application usage is unblocked. The wind-down (c5903c15) no longer holds these two lanes.\nAdopted: the general rule. A live scope's retained state is a function of its current items, not of how many ticks ran. There is no declared renewal form, and the validator does not change. Four parts, with one change to your proposal:\n1. Retry record: key it by (actor, target item), not by actor alone. One key can act on two items, such as a cursor and a card. Keyed by actor alone, the second act evicts the first act's record, and a retry of the first act is judged fresh. Without an expected revision, that applies it twice. An act that creates an item keys by the item it creates. A new act by the same actor on the same item replaces the record. An exact retry of the latest act answers applied with its original tick and no byte change. The same key with a different intent answers bad-intent (idempotency-mismatch). A repeat of a superseded act is judged fresh against current state. Recorded applyEntry keeps full retention unchanged.\n2. Fixed hashes: drop them after seq 1 in applyLive and in liveTimedAppend. First add a test that fails if any live path seals or reads a fixed hash after seq 1, and show it red against a deliberate seal before the change.\n3. Final items: evict them in this change, with their retry records. Without eviction, churn still fills the scope in about 150 hours at 50 members. The note states what a read and an act naming an evicted item answer, including a retry of the leave that ended it. PB-3 treats that answer on a leave retry as left.\n4. Detached text: skip putTexts growth in applyLive. Distinct acting keys stay as they are, bounded at 4,096 per run.\nClient rule for the note: a live client keeps at most one unanswered act per (actor, item). PB-3 already retries one key until answered and sends an expected revision on each renewal.\nOrder: first the amendment to notes/2026-11-10-live-level.md as a notes-only head with a short checker review. Then the source in state.ts, fold.ts, live-envelope.ts and live-meter.ts, with a full gate and kernel review under docs/kernel.md. Acceptance: at 50 members and 15 seconds, retained bytes after 1,000 renewals equal those after 10, and a churn run of leave and re-enter returns to the same total. State the wake rate (no alarm is added) in the review.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}